    {
      "id": "9df9bf0472bbff919d468c1539acc4b0d7937deb",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 554469056,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I'm not entirely sure that's the place to put it.  Most of the stuff under \"Layout\" is concerned with the way the main window is, well, laid out, and the hover-coloring isn't entirely obviously concerned with that.\n\nI'm also not sure there's any other place that's obviously better.\n\n(This is as much a matter of [discoverability](https://www.interaction-design.org/literature/article/make-it-easy-on-the-user-designing-for-discoverability-within-mobile-apps) as anything else - ideally, the knob for a feature should be in the \"most obvious place\", so that users, ideally, find it in the first place they look.  Unfortunately, that requires either guessing, or measuring with a pile of test users, what the first place they'd look for it is.)\n\n*Some* UI preference settings might belong in the View menu, although *that* runs the risk of a View menu that has to support scrolling even on normal users' screens....\n\nSo maybe we should leave it in the Layout pane for now, and see what happens.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
